  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Soliris (eculizumab) / Ultomiris (ravulizumab-cwvz) Criteria Version 2; Original 2/24/22; Approval 9/16/2022; Effective 11/01/2022.",
    "All four approval branches and shared vaccine, specialty, and prescriber REMS denial gates are encoded. Diagnosis is attested by the closed indication. Approval section permits Soliris or Ultomiris for gMG, although the FDA indications paragraph names only Soliris for gMG. NMOSD is Soliris only.",
    "Age follows this PDF: at least 1 month for aHUS/PNH, represented as 1/12 age_years; at least 18 years for gMG/NMOSD. UI band minima preserve these thresholds.",
    "gMG immunosuppressive examples: azathioprine, mycophenolate mofetil, cyclosporine, cyclophosphamide, methotrexate, tacrolimus, rituximab. No specific agent picklist is required.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 4 months; reauthorization up to 12 months if prescriber documents disease improvement.",
    "Quantity (notes only): Soliris max dose 1200 mg; J1300 max HCPCS 120. Ultomiris max dose 3600 mg; J1303 max HCPCS 360. Product-specific limits require manual review; max_units is null.",
    "Cautions (notes only): see package inserts https://solirispro.com/pdf/Soliris_USPI.pdf and https://alexion.com/Documents/Ultomiris_USPI.pdf .",
    "PDL status unknown. Empaveli is a related complement inhibitor alternative for PNH overlap only; its own criteria require separate review.",
    "Remains partial: laboratory and treatment-history evidence is attested; documentation, duration, reauthorization improvement, quantity/dosing, and package-insert cautions require manual review. PNH requires all three baseline values, without an invented hemoglobin threshold."
  ],
